## 2026-08-27 — Combat reshape: guns replace the sword

Full design + as-built detail in
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-guns-design.md`.

**Why.** `SwordCombat`'s joust was a coin flip, not a duel: `BaseDmg 35` ×
`SpeedDmgScale` at `SpeedForMaxDmg 16` — which is exactly `BhopMaxSpeed` — × the
1.5× head multiplier = 123 damage against 100 HP. A full-speed bhop headshot was a
**one-shot**, so whoever landed the first pass won and the 40 s hunt phase was
decided in one exchange. Guns turn TTK into a tunable dial and move the skill
expression onto the movement system, which is the strongest part of the project.

**Shape.** Random gun from a starter pool on spawn, random gun from an arena pool
as the middle prize; the host rolls both once and broadcasts, so both players get
identical weapons. Player-only — training bots keep their swords, so
`EnemyController`'s combat was not rewritten.

**Key discoveries worth remembering:**

- **Damage was already client-authoritative** (`{"t":"hit","dmg":X}` relayed off
  `PlayerHealth.DamageDealt` on the local puppet). Hitscan and rocket splash both
  fit that contract with *zero* new damage netcode — only two cosmetic messages
  (`shot`, `reload`) were added.
- **UAL1 already shipped a full pistol animation set** that had never been wired
  up: `Pistol_Idle`, `Pistol_Shoot`, `Pistol_Reload`, and an
  `Pistol_Aim_Up/Neutral/Down` trio now feeding a `BlendSpace1D` off camera pitch.
  `Hit_Head` / `Hit_Chest` were sitting unused too.
- **Godot's GLTF importer strips a trailing `_Loop` from animation names.** The
  clip is `Pistol_Idle_Loop` in the GLB but imports as `Pistol_Idle`; mapping the
  file name silently failed to resolve. This is also why `Idle_Loop` has always
  been referenced as `Idle`.
- **The Styloo gun pack has no animation clips, but every gun is modelled in
  separate parts** (slide/bolt, magazine, trigger, and the shotgun's pump). Driving
  those procedurally off `GunCombat`'s own fire/reload timers is *better* than
  baked clips — it stays locked to whatever numbers are tuned.
- **Every Styloo gun is modelled barrel-along-+X**, so viewmodel and hand model
  both need `+90°` Y to point the muzzle down `-Z`. `test/TestGunOrient.tscn`
  asserts this per gun.
- **Bug fixed: AABB measuring must apply node transforms.** The first helper merged
  mesh-local AABBs directly, which mis-measures any multi-part model (the rocket
  launcher read 0.85 m instead of 1.18 m) and threw off viewmodel scaling. Now one
  shared `GunCombat.MeasureAabb` walks the hierarchy accumulating transforms.
- **Balance caught by the new harness, not by feel.** The first pass had MAC-10 at
  0.52 s and AK-47 at 0.42 s TTK — below human reaction time, i.e. the sword's
  exact flaw again. Slowing two fire intervals fixed it.

**Testing.** `test/TestGunRange.tscn` sweeps every gun × 3 distances headless and
prints shots-and-seconds to kill; `test/TestGunOrient.tscn` is a one-screenshot
orientation check-sheet. All gun numbers are `[Export]`ed for live inspector
tuning without a rebuild.

**Also added:** reload ring (hidden until you reload, sweeps over the real reload
duration), ammo counter, spread-reactive crosshair, and full reticle customisation
in Settings (colour / size / gap / thickness / centre dot, persisted).

**Audio is wired but silent** until four WAVs are dropped into
`assets/audio/sfx/combat/`: `GunShotLight`, `GunShotHeavy`, `GunReload`,
`GunDryFire`. Missing files are silent no-ops, not errors.

**Unrelated pre-existing breakage found:** `test/TestPieceCategories.cs` is
untracked scratch referencing `PieceDB.CategoryOf`, which has never existed at
HEAD — it was failing the *entire* project build. Parked as `.cs.disabled`.

